"GUIDE_HEADER" = "Wallpapers / New / CarPlay / Settings";
"GUIDE_STEP1_BODY" = "In CarPlay Settings → Wallpaper, select each of the six patterned wallpapers in the top and middle rows once. Solid colors do not create these cache files. In CarCanvas → CarPlay, tap Retry to load the groups and their previews.";
"GUIDE_STEP1_TITLE" = "Prepare the CarPlay cache";
"GUIDE_STEP2_BODY" = "Tap the Dark and Light preview slots separately to choose a photo for each. The photos may be different. Enter a file name and create the wallpaper; both CPBitmap files are saved as one group in Wallpapers. Creation alone does not change CarPlay.";
"GUIDE_STEP2_TITLE" = "New: choose two photos";
"GUIDE_STEP3_BODY" = "Tap Apply on your wallpaper, choose one existing CarPlay cache group using its previews and filenames, and confirm. Dark and Light photos replace only the corresponding existing members of that group; other colors and numeric suffixes are not changed. Then log out from Wallpapers or Settings so CarPlay reloads the cache.";
"GUIDE_STEP3_TITLE" = "Wallpapers: apply one group";
"GUIDE_STEP4_BODY" = "Backups are below the cache groups on CarPlay. The first scan saves each cache file before it can be overwritten. Tap Restore for a valid backup to restore that exact filename, then log out. Legacy or recovered copies are labeled and are not guaranteed to contain the system original.";
"GUIDE_STEP4_TITLE" = "CarPlay: backups and restore";
